from the HunterPie project, Copyright the HunterPie contributors, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

    https://github.com/HunterPie/HunterPie

The .map files are plain-text tables of static addresses and pointer offsets
that HunterPie obtained through reverse engineering of Monster Hunter: World,
Monster Hunter Rise and Monster Hunter Wilds. They are redistributed here
unmodified.

The file crates/mh-overlay-games/src/tables.rs is generated by
scripts/generate_tables.py from HunterPie's MonsterData.xml for World and Rise
(capture thresholds, part lists and ailment ids) and from the HunterPie
localization repository's es-es.xml (monster, part and ailment names). It is a
derived subset of that data, not a copy of the XML. The localization files are
Copyright the HunterPie contributors, licensed under the MIT License:

    https://github.com/HunterPie/localization

The file crates/mh-overlay-games/src/buffs.rs is a hand-written derivative of
HunterPie's AbnormalityData.xml for World (buff and debuff offsets, their
depends-on/value pairs, and the flags for infinite buffs). The names are
Spanish translations of that file's ABNORMALITY_* keys, not copies of the
game's localization.

No source code from HunterPie is included; the Rust implementation in this
repository was written independently against the observed memory layout.
Weapon gauge offsets (spirit, phials, switch axe, demon mode, kinsect) come
from HunterPie's MHW structure definitions, used as reference values only.

